From 43ae75184665e47b1d7fdb79fdb30081af3b4c19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joris-sta <joris-sta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:45:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kv: per-layer q8_0 cache pinning (--kv-q8-layers) on the
 fixed-type path

New public option --kv-q8-layers <LIST> (indices or inclusive ranges,
e.g. 3,7,11-15) pins BOTH K and V of selected zero-based model layers to
q8_0 while sibling layers keep -ctk/-ctv. Recurrent and sliding-window
layers are rejected, indices must be existing full-attention layers,
duplicates deduplicate, and all callers (server, bench, CLI) share one
strict parser (common_parse_kv_q8_layers). Dynamic VBR is refused on the
same context so selected layers cannot silently degrade; shared/reused
cache layers and VBR env overrides also conflict and are rejected at
init. The public context API gains kv_q8_layers / n_kv_q8_layers and is
copied at context creation.

Also carried in the params plumbing: --checkpoint-max-mib (per-checkpoint
capture cap, -1 inherits --cache-ram, 0 disables), --resume-max-mib and
--resume-budget-path for the persistent resume disk budget, a server fit
guard that refuses unproven automatic placements when auxiliary models
cannot fit, and llama-bench's kv choice plumbing for VBR arms.
